  "lineage": "The Paiwan of the Pingtung and Taitung hills sing songs in which a leader's melody runs over a drone held by the group, and play the double nose flute (lalingedan), usually with one pipe fingered for the melody over a second pipe that sounds mainly a drone; the nose flute, a man's instrument associated with courtship and mourning, and the double mouth flute are registered in Taiwan as an Important Traditional Performing Art. The tongali card stands in for the Paiwan nose flute.",
